1:38:29Z","updated_at":"2026-05-22T14:51:16Z","closed_at":"2026-05-22T14:51:10Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in: v4.6.2.stable.official [71f334935], v4.6.3.stable.official [7d41c59c4]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.3.stable - Windows 11 (build 26200) - Single-window, 1 monitor - Direct3D 12 (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3050 Laptop GPU (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.9579) - 11th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-11300H @ 3.10GHz (8 threads) - 15.69 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nDecals glitch visually and rectangular chunks of them disappear in screen space. It appears to be dependant on transforms of the decal aswell. Scaling or extending the decal sufficiently tends to snap the glitch away in an instand beyond a certain threshold. I've tried various configurations but nothing seems to fix it. Issue may be more difficult to reproduce with decals not pointing straight downwards.\n\nIt occurs when the scale of decal is non-uniform.\n\nUniform scale :\n<img width=\"599\" height=\"414\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/159584d2-88ad-46a0-b991-84ed07b3c97a\" />\n\nNon-uniform scale :\n<img width=\"603\" height=\"419\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/65c8696a-731f-4a6e-b183-0047b59b0848\" />\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1 - Add a decal to the scene\n2 - Give it an Albedo Texture\n3 - Scale the decal to 4.0 scale along x and z axis while keeping y axis in 1.0 scale (this maximizes the visibility of the issue)\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nMRP not required, very easy to replicate in a fresh empty project.","closed_by":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://